      "problem": "The domain of the function $f(x)$ is $-3\\lt x \\leq 3$ and the range of $f$ is $-2\\leq f(x) \\lt 2.$ What is the range of the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-3\\lt x \\leq 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-3\\lt  f^{-1}(x) \\leq 3.\n$$",
